alMs","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"heartbeat_interval_ms is the interval, in milliseconds, at which this"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stream asks the server to send a WatchHeartbeat while it is idle. 0, which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is also what an SDK older than the heartbeat leaves here, asks for none:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"such a stream gets no WatchHeartbeat bodies at all, so the heartbeat can"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"never reach a client that would not recognize it. The server clamps the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"request to its own bounds and reports the value it settled on in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"WatchInitialization.heartbeat_interval_ms."}],"url":"\/documentation\/yorkie\/yorkie_v1_watchrequest\/heartbeatintervalms","role":"symbol"},"doc://Yorkie/documentation/Yorkie/Yorkie_V1_WatchRequest/resources":{"url":"\/documentation\/yorkie\/yorkie_v1_watchrequest\/resources","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie\/Yorkie_V1_WatchRequest\/resources","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"resources","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Yorkie_V1_ResourceDescriptor","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Yorkie0A22_V1_ResourceDescriptorV"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"resources","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"resources lists what the stream delivers. It must hold between 1 and 100"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"descriptors, and the server must recognize every one of them: a request"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"naming a resource the server cannot subscribe to is rejected whole rather"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than served in part, so a client never watches fewer 